Build the SPIRV-LLVM-Translator from a local source directory.

AdaptiveCpp's ExternalProject fetches the translator over git at configure
time; conda builds must be reproducible and offline-capable, so point the
sub-build at the pre-fetched, pinned source tree instead
(FETCHCONTENT-style redirect via LLVMSPIRV_SOURCE_DIR, which the recipe
seeds from the SPIRV-LLVM-Translator source entry).

Context is kept to the ExternalProject_Add line only: the surrounding
lines differ between the release pin and develop (develop gained
LLVMSPIRV_EXECUTABLE_NAME and its own CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE forwarding).

diff --git a/src/compiler/llvm-to-backend/CMakeLists.txt b/src/compiler/llvm-to-backend/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/compiler/llvm-to-backend/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/compiler/llvm-to-backend/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -196,6 +196,3 @@
     ExternalProject_Add(LLVMSpirvTranslator
-      GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/AdaptiveCpp/SPIRV-LLVM-Translator
-      GIT_TAG origin/${LLVMSPIRV_BRANCH}
-      GIT_SHALLOW ON
-      GIT_REMOTE_UPDATE_STRATEGY CHECKOUT
+      SOURCE_DIR ${LLVMSPIRV_SOURCE_DIR}
       BUILD_ALWAYS OFF
